# n8n behind one reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Traefik or one load balancer).
# Both lines are the ones n8n's "Configure webhook URLs with reverse proxy" page sets.
#
# N8N_WEBHOOK_URL — without it the Webhook node shows http://localhost:5678/... (tested with n8n 2.41.3's UrlService).
#   N8N_EDITOR_BASE_URL alone fixes only the TEST webhook URL; the production one stays localhost.
#   WEBHOOK_URL (old name) still works but is deprecated from 2.35.0 and logs a warning at startup.
# N8N_PROXY_HOPS — number of proxies you control in front of n8n. Without it, a proxy that sends X-Forwarded-For
#   makes n8n (NODE_ENV=production) log ERR_ERL_UNEXPECTED_X_FORWARDED_FOR, and every user shares the proxy's IP
#   in the login / password-reset rate limits (we got a 429 on the 6th password-reset check from one IP).
#   Do not set it higher than the real number of proxies.
N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=https://n8n.example.com/
N8N_PROXY_HOPS=1
